            standing: Ours,
            as_read: "copper for all potable water; no PVC or other synthetics that leach toxins",
            source: [Ours("the operator's rule recorded in conduits.rs (v0.535): no PVC or other synthetics that leach toxins")],
            note: "THIS SHIP'S rule, not law: the editor shows it as the ship's rule. An open question for the operator (design section 19, question 2: copper only, or anything a code allows, now that a run's material can change); this one row is the whole of it, so it stays reversible. Hot water is drinking water heated (the water heater is fed from the purifier), so it is copper too.",
